       _m_u_l_t_i  Valid values are _o_n and _o_f_f.  If set to _o_n, the resolver library
              will return all valid addresses for a host that appears  in  the
              _/_e_t_c_/_h_o_s_t_s  file, instead of only the first.  This is _o_f_f by de‐
              fault, as it may cause a substantial performance loss  at  sites
              with large hosts files.

       _r_e_o_r_d_e_r
              Valid values are _o_n and _o_f_f.  If set to _o_n, the resolver library
              will  attempt  to reorder host addresses so that local addresses
              (i.e., on the same subnet) are listed first  when  a  ggeetthhoossttbbyy‐‐
              nnaammee(3)  is  performed.  Reordering is done for all lookup meth‐
              ods.  The default value is _o_f_f.

